{"aligned_passages":[],"lenses":{},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=a95759ce5c96e8226b9411d42d1138f4b439d3c1a2e4ebf7160579b702e450e1&ref=sha256%3A5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1%2Fevidence%2Fmapping.long.lem-denominator-sandwich","record":{"command":[],"details":"The papers' evidence mapping names these Lean declarations for Long record Lemma 6.55 (The odd denominator survives dyadic subtraction). Long record lem:denominator-sandwich: lean.status exact_or_stronger. Relation note: The Lean statements take integers $p,r$ with no sign condition on $p/2^c-r/D$. `dyadicResidualIntNumerator_coprime_oddDenominator` shows that $pD-2^cr$ is coprime to $D$ when $D$ is odd and $\\gcd(r,D)=1$, and `dyadicResidualInt_denominator_sandwich` then gives both divisibilities for the reduced denominator of $(pD-2^cr)/(2^cD)$, so the printed lemma is their one-line composition. `dyadicResidual_denominator_sandwich` is the special case $p,r\\ge0$ with $2^cr\\le pD$. Sources: evidence/paper_evidence.json at 3368d1e69467. Scope: copied from the papers' evidence mapping; this example did not review the correspondence.","id":"mapping.long.lem-denominator-sandwich","kind":"semantic_review","source_ids":["evidence_mapping"],"status":"not_run","subject_ids":["lean.Erdos249257.dyadicResidualIntNumerator_coprime_oddDenominator","lean.Erdos249257.dyadicResidualInt_denominator_sandwich","lean.Erdos249257.dyadicResidual_denominator_sandwich","long.lem-denominator-sandwich"],"tool":"Copied from the papers' evidence mapping (plectis-paper-evidence/2); no review by this example"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/evidence/mapping.long.lem-denominator-sandwich","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/evidence/mapping.long.lem-denominator-sandwich","id":"field:09c1f8497485e1fedac8d3f3fd69938a228bc4db794ce7c2740945491c8c9